From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:45:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Mac: a Pro Controller clone read as raw HID takes report
 0x3F's buttons, full sticks and its player lights

Builds on #859, which reads pads of other vendors as raw HID: a PowerA NANO pairs over
Bluetooth as "Lic Pro Controller", HID vendor and product 0, and GameController never lists it.

Such a pad stays in the Pro Controller's simple report 0x3F. Buttons in that report take its
numbering, read from the device's elements and not from a name or vendor. Its sticks are raw,
so pad_hid_raw_axis measures them from their rest against the reach seen so far: a full push
gave 61 to 74% and now gives 99 to 100%. The pad also gets its player on its lights
(subcommand 0x30), which it otherwise chases until a console gives it one.

Played in FINAL FANTASY RESONANCE with the NANO on #859 plus this change: it connects at
once as player 1, its buttons are in place, full tilt runs and player 1's light is on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#989
Reason: Map Nintendo report 0x3F buttons, calibrate PowerA sticks and set player lights.
Issue: seedds/nxnative#989
